# the three layouts: Pan (zigzag, right first, as makers lay a pan out), Pan rev (left first), Linear (low
# to high); the ding's
# keys dim-lit; Just tuning over the ding
# (params: 23 Layout 33 Tuning; keys: 0 F3 .. 26 G5; white 7 is key 12, white 8 key 14, white 2 key 4;
# the white key at each end: the steel, in every layout; the ding's own field beside its keys)
wait 1600
expect par23 0
expect dimkey 14
tap SEL
spin K1 1
expect par23 1
expect white8 5000
expect white5 5700
expect white10 5800
expect white1 7200
expect white14 7400
expect white6 -1
expect white15 -1
wait 50
shot pan_rev.png
spin K1 1
expect par23 2
expect white0 -1
expect white1 -1
expect white2 5000
expect white3 -1
expect white4 5700
expect white9 6500
expect white14 7600
wait 30
expect dimkey 4
shot linear.png
tapkey w2
tapkey w4
tapkey w5
wait 50
expect note5700 >5
spin K1 -2
expect par23 0
# Just: the fifth over the ding pure (A3 two cents sharp of equal), E (9/8) 4 sharp, C (9/5) 18 sharp
tap ENV
spin K3 1
expect par33 1
expect white10 5702
expect white12 6404
expect white11 6018
tapkey w10
wait 30
expect note5702 >5
spin K3 -1
expect white10 5700
# the scales wrap round: one back from Kurd is SaByeD, in E: E3 / A3 B3 C#4 ... (its G# and D# named so)
tap SEL
turn ALGO -1
expect par24 10
expect par25 4
expect white8 5200
expect white10 5700
expect white5 5900
expect white11 6100
wait 50
shot sabyed.png
